<urn:atm:triage:finding/FTQ-002>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "FTQ-002" ;
  triage:title "Flaky real-wall-clock sleep race in peer-connection-pool eviction test instead of paused-clock pattern" ;
  triage:description "Test `expired_idle_connection_is_evicted_and_redialed` in crates/atm-http-runtime/src/peer_connection_pool.rs:909-940 is declared `#[tokio::test]` (not `#[tokio::test(start_paused = true)]`), configures `idle_timeout=5ms`, then does a real `tokio::time::sleep(15ms)` (a fixed 3x race margin) before calling `evict_idle_now()` and asserting eviction counts. This is a real-wall-clock timing race, not the deterministic `start_paused = true` + `tokio::time::advance()` pattern already used elsewhere in this same AO2 phase's code (e.g. client.rs's `request_deadline_bounds_the_connector_once`). Under CI contention/slow runners the 3x margin can still flake. Fix: convert the test to `#[tokio::test(start_paused = true)]` and use `tokio::time::advance(Duration::from_millis(...))` instead of a real sleep, matching the existing pattern in this codebase." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-ao2" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "flaky-test" ;
  triage:severity "important" ;
  triage:repeatable true ;
  triage:sweepScope "file_only" ;
  triage:status "fixed" ;
  triage:dispatchReady true ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-08-26T07:30:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:foundIn triage:AO2.15 ;
  triage:foundAt "2026-08-26T06:45:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/FTQ-002/FTQ-002-occ-1> ;
  triage:triageRecordVersion "1" .

